# Line endings that do not depend on who cloned the repository.
#
# `core.autocrlf=true` is the default on Windows, so without these rules the
# committed git hooks are checked out with CRLF. bash then fails on the first
# line of the script (`set: -\n: invalid option`), the gate never runs, and
# tests/test_r2_gate_wiring.py::test_hooks_fail_closed is red on a clean
# Windows checkout. Anything bash executes is therefore pinned to LF.
.githooks/* text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf

# Interpreted by the Windows shells, which want CRLF.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
